## threshold-t1 | always | independent | section 1 table, row 1 "Non-novel chemical/biological weapons production"
"non_novel_chem_bio_weapons" is listed.
## threshold-t2 | always | independent | section 1 table, row 2 "Novel chemical/biological weapons production"
"novel_chem_bio_weapons" is listed.
## threshold-t3 | always | independent | section 1 table, row 3 "Misaligned AI systems in high-stakes settings"
"misaligned_high_stakes" is listed.
## threshold-t4 | always | independent | section 1 table, row 4 "Automated R&D in key domains"
"automated_rd" is listed.
## highly-capable-t4 | always | independent | 3.6 "A model is 'highly capable' if we conclude that it crosses the threshold for automated AI R&D described in Section 1"
For every situation that has crossed "automated_rd", that situation is classified as "highly_capable".
## t4-suff | always | RS0 | row T4 "We will consider this threshold to be met if we determine that either (1) our models would be able to fully substitute for our entire set of Research Scientists and Research Engineers, at competitive costs (i.e., within a factor of 5); or (2) there is “dramatic acceleration” of the pace of AI progress for reasons that likely relate to the automation of AI R&D." (RS3o suff and iff both state it; "if we determine" governs both branches: full_substitution_at_competitive_cost and scenario_2 are each the company's determination)
For every situation that is classified as "full_substitution_at_competitive_cost", that situation has crossed "automated_rd". For every situation that is classified as "scenario_2", that situation has crossed "automated_rd".
## t4-only-if | RS3o=iff | RS0 | row T4, the same definition read as complete (RS3o iff adds the converse)
For every situation that has crossed "automated_rd", either that situation is classified as "full_substitution_at_competitive_cost" or that situation is classified as "scenario_2", or both.
## s2-suff-third | always | RS0 | row T4 "We would consider scenario (2) to have occurred where (a) we observe or expect double the rate of progress ... and (b) it is plausible that this doubling is substantially attributable to the automation of research and/or engineering" with "such that continuation of the trend in AI progress seems likely to lead to even greater acceleration" as a third condition (formerly RS3c third; the reading "result" is excluded by the v3.4 changelog, PLAN 12)
For every situation that is classified as "double_rate" and that is classified as "automation_attributable", if that situation is classified as "continuation_accelerates", then that situation is classified as "scenario_2".
## s2-only-if-third | RS3i=iff | RS0 | scenario (2)'s definition read as complete, three conditions
For every situation that is classified as "scenario_2", that situation is classified as "double_rate". For every situation that is classified as "scenario_2", that situation is classified as "automation_attributable". For every situation that is classified as "scenario_2", that situation is classified as "continuation_accelerates".
